            compare: "Ring-enhancing lesions have a short differential: abscess, necrotic primary tumor or metastasis, toxoplasmosis and other opportunistic infections, and occasionally tumefactive demyelination. Restricted diffusion in the center and a clear infective source favor abscess; a necrotic tumor usually has a center that does not restrict.",
            deeper: "The likely organisms follow the source: streptococci and anaerobes from teeth and sinuses, Staphylococcus aureus after trauma or surgery or from endocarditis. In immunosuppressed patients the range widens to Toxoplasma, Nocardia, fungi, and mycobacteria, which is why aspirated material is sent for a broad range of tests.",
