      modelAnswer: "Progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy (PML) from JC virus.",
      rationale: "[[progressive-multifocal-leukoencephalopathy|Progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy]] is JC virus infection of [[oligodendrocyte|oligodendrocytes]] in people with impaired immunity, including those taking natalizumab. It causes focal deficits that progress over weeks, with asymmetric white matter lesions that typically lack mass effect and, in the classic form, enhancement. JC virus PCR in the CSF with compatible clinical and MRI findings supports the diagnosis; treatment means restoring immune function (here, stopping natalizumab).",
